"""Build local user guide and a fresh, credential-free Chat handover; never controls CFD."""
from pathlib import Path
import html,json,datetime
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;B=R.parent;D=B/'dashboard_work_20261030'
def read(p):
 try:return json.loads(Path(p).read_text(encoding='utf-8-sig'))
 except (OSError,ValueError):return {}
def build():
 import local_control_model as m
 now=datetime.datetime.now().astimezone().isoformat();state=read(R/'wave_foil_run_state.json');hold=m.hold()
 try:selected=m.mesh_inputs().selected()
 except Exception:selected=None
 active=state.get('computation_active') is True
 current=Path(state.get('directory','missing'));latest=read(current/'latest_checkpoint.json')
 snap=dict(updated_at=now,campaign_hold=hold,current_case=state.get('case'),computation_active=active,physical_progress=state.get('progress'),selected_mesh=selected,latest_checkpoint=latest,readiness=m.readiness(),queue=[dict(id=j.get('id'),status=j.get('status'),spec=j.get('spec'),message=j.get('message'),resume_manifest=j.get('resume_manifest')) for j in m.jobs()],current_diagnostics=read(current/'diagnostic_summary.json'),previous_guard_review=str(R/'c01_calm_r2_guard_review.json'))
 prompt="""Continue the NTNU quasi-2D campaign from current DISK STATE, not this snapshot.
The operator can paste a prepared M11/later .sim path in the local dashboard. Inspecting or selecting a mesh does not run flow. Imported source files are copied immutably into a new E: attempt and never overwritten. The selected mesh is a mechanically checked candidate, not a convergence-approved mesh.
WORK RESERVE: the user reported about10% remaining and requested7% kept for emergency fixes. After this handover stop autonomous development in this chat; use the local control panel manually. An agent must not claim exact remaining usage because it is not visible here.
CURRENT USER HOLD: our C01 and waves are paused pending the other agent's mesh convergence/optimization review. Do not launch or release this hold without an explicit later user instruction. Leave the separate mesh-study and HF sessions untouched.
The independent M10-M12 mesh study also has dedicated Pause & save / Resume saved calculation buttons. mesh_study_control.py manages only that study, uses its STOP marker and waits for verified final.sim/export/process exit. Resume creates a new attempt and keeps prior histories; never restart gpu_calm_study_live.py directly. See mesh_control_receipt.json for isolated test scope; no live pause/resume was performed during installation.
Read RESUME_AT_HOME.txt, campaign_hold.json, local_control_model.py, current jobs and actual process/lock state first. Never duplicate/restart a completed controller.
Open http://127.0.0.1:8771/ or double-click Open_NTNU_Control.cmd in F:/ntnu/mesh_screening_20261028. Starting this service never launches CFD.
Workflow: paste mesh .sim path -> zero-flow inspect -> select imported candidate -> configure wave/domain -> save queue (no launch) -> explicit release hold and Start. If requested, Check recipe performs only CPU1 zero-step new-wave and saved-wave API checks. New domain or mesh gets its own fresh flat-water C01; do not use old imported fields as a settled baseline.
CL means (vertical force - buoyancy)/(0.5*rho_ref*U_ref^2*A_ref). Use the audited per-case force_reference.json derived from native rho/gravity and actual closed foil geometry. Keep raw Fz/CL_total immutable. No guessed global correction for an imported mesh; unavailable evidence must block corrected-lift acceptance. Historical raw-CL decisions remain explicitly historical. C01 settling: adjacent complete0.2s means CD and corrected CL each change<0.5%; retain source/finite/phase/speed guards. Wave: FifthOrder, full inlet height from activation with no ramp, no global wave reinitialization; preserve original wave clock on resume. Near-foil wave establishment precedes four-cycle repeatability review. Ten periods is an expectation, not a minimum;20 periods from activation is a review cap.
Geometry: z=-22..8m, waterline2m, depth24m+air6m, U18m/s, foil geometry/location unchanged, one20mm span. H.25/.5/.75; lambda10/20/30/40; planned originalW01a.5/20,W02.5/30,3lambda/4lambda then boundedextras. Selected file's supported dt0.0001..0.001s is retained; no silent1ms reset. Ten inner, SO; startup uses40steps at min(dt,.5ms)/50inner then restoresdt/10.
Physical speed guard50m/s and bounded phase remain. Phase mass0.01% review flag remains visible; user allowed exploratory mass deviation, not physical guard failure. No force-accuracy claim from repeatability alone.
Stop/save pauses the queue; wait for a completed saved checkpoint. Continue saved run creates a new attempt from a verified normal-stop/wall-limit final save and retains original wave clock/history. Guard-failed or interrupted-startup fields cannot be resumed this way.
Frequent checkpoints default0.05s (configurable.05-1s), all saved attempts preserved; disk/RAM guards apply. Never continue the failed C01r2 final at2.777s. Its airspeed50.162m/s is diagnostic, not a settled baseline.
Standalone controls: local_control_model.py, local_control_worker.py, local_mesh_inputs.py, local_domain_preparation.py, local_recipe_validation.py, LocalCalmWave.java, PrepareLocalMeshCalm.java, manual_control_server.py. Compile/controller tests and actual zero-flow STAR API checks have separate receipts. Read local_control_zero_step_review.json and check_recipe_final_review.json for current macro identity and tested scope; an API pass does not validate C01/wave flow or a new mesh. Do not forge readiness or mark a selected mesh converged.
Dashboard: technical status and controls, Mesh assessment / Waves, then archive and combined results. A completed or stopped run leaves the live area and enters a collapsed archive; no old case values remain in the idle live template. Resuming uses only verified matching history; a new wave starts a separate record. Mesh view includes actual mesh and pressure/streamline previews with source/time provenance. Report: local_campaign_results.html supports saved-case selection, buoyancy-corrected CL/CD histories, cycle overlap/convergence, diagnostics and source paths. Live case remains in dashboard.html. Both reports explicitly distinguish failed, paused, exploratory and repeatable results.
Update handover and reports on meaningful state changes; never expose licensing/service credentials.
"""
 text=prompt+"\nSnapshot (verify live files before action):\n"+json.dumps(snap,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False,default=str)
 (R/'CHAT_CONTINUE_LATEST.txt').write_text(text,encoding='utf8')
 (R/'standalone_handover_snapshot.json').write_text(json.dumps(snap,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False,default=str),encoding='utf8')
 style='body{font:16px/1.6 system-ui;color:#18394d;max-width:1050px;margin:30px auto;padding:18px}h1{font-size:28px}h2{font-size:21px;margin-top:28px}a{color:#056b99}code,textarea{overflow-wrap:anywhere}code{font-size:13px;white-space:normal}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%}th,td{border-bottom:1px solid #ccd8df;text-align:left;padding:12px;vertical-align:top}textarea{box-sizing:border-box;width:100%;height:55vh;font:13px/1.5 monospace}button{padding:10px 16px;background:#17648a;color:white;border:0;cursor:pointer}.note{padding:14px;background:#edf5f8;border-left:4px solid #17648a}.warn{background:#fff3e8;border-color:#a94725}@media(max-width:600px){body{font-size:14px}th,td{padding:7px}h1{font-size:23px}}@media print{button,textarea{display:none}body{margin:0;font-size:10pt}.note{break-inside:avoid}}'
 header=lambda title:'<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>'+title+'</title><style>'+style+'</style></head><body>'
 guide=header('Standalone simulation control')+"""<p><a href="dashboard.html#manual-control-panel">Back to local controls</a> · <a href="local_campaign_results.html">Combined results</a> · <a href="chat_rescue.html">Chat rescue</a></p><h1>Continue without an active Work session</h1><p>The local Python service, controller and STAR macros run on this computer. Keep the computer powered and awake. Opening the dashboard starts no calculation.</p>
<div class="note"><b>Current campaign:</b> """+html.escape(hold.get('reason','No campaign hold recorded'))+"""</div>
<h2>1. Point to your prepared mesh</h2><p>Paste an absolute path to an existing <code>.sim</code>, for example your M11 file, and click <b>Inspect mesh</b>. This creates a separate copy on E: and performs a CPU inspection with zero flow steps. It records cell count, domain, timestep, boundary names, quality and one-span topology. The source file stays untouched. Wait for the inspection result, then select the imported copy.</p><p>Mechanical compatibility does not establish mesh convergence. Review the other agent's study before enabling flow. Unsupported inputs display what needs to be changed; edit a separate file in STAR and inspect it as a new input.</p>
<h2>2. Choose a wave and domain</h2><p>Select H, wavelength, upstream/downstream distances, wall-time limit and checkpoint interval. The timestep is read from the selected file. A new mesh, domain or numerical profile requires its own C01. The local builder preserves the selected foil/prism coordinates and checks the new remote geometry before any flow. It initializes a fresh flat-water copy; previous imported fields do not count as settled C01.</p>
<h2>3. Save the queue, then enable it explicitly</h2><p><b>Save configuration</b> only records a request. <b>Release campaign hold</b> only enables future starts. Neither starts a solver. If the readiness list requests it, <b>Check recipe</b> performs a separate zero-flow CPU API inspection. Once the checks pass and you are ready, click <b>Start queued jobs</b>. The sequence is matching C01, computed settled save, full-height inlet wave, cycle assessment and saved result.</p>
<h2>4. Watch, stop and continue</h2><p><b>Current mesh study:</b> use the separate <a href="dashboard.html#mesh-run-controls">Mesh calculation pause and resume</a> buttons near the top. Pause finishes the current step and saves. Wait for <b>Paused and saved</b> before unplugging. Resume continues the saved mesh campaign with its existing settings and histories; it does not release the separate wave-campaign hold.</p><p>The main dashboard shows the current case, CL/CD, latest physical time, arrival/period estimates, saved side view, CPU/GPU state and diagnostics. A view labelled with a saved time is a snapshot, not a continuous field animation.</p><p><b>Stop, save and pause queue</b> waits for a step boundary and writes the calculated fields. Do not disconnect power before the saved file appears. <b>Continue saved run</b> queues a new attempt from a verified normal-stop checkpoint; press Start separately. A physical-guard failure cannot use ordinary continuation.</p><p>Checkpoints default to every0.05s of simulated time. Frequent full .sim files use disk space and add save time; the controller stops if resources become insufficient. You can choose0.05-1s for future jobs.</p>
<h2>5. Select results in the combined report</h2><p>Use <b>Mesh assessment</b> for mesh, pressure and streamline previews. Use <b>Waves</b> for the current CL/CD history, cycle overlays, convergence and the saved free surface. Finished or stopped runs move to the collapsed archive and leave the live area ready for the next case.</p><p><b>CL excludes buoyancy:</b> the audited hydrostatic buoyancy is subtracted from vertical force before normalization. The original force and CL_total history remain preserved. If the case lacks verified geometry or physical reference values, corrected CL is unavailable rather than estimated.</p><p><a href="local_campaign_results.html">Open the combined report</a> and choose the cases to display. Use CL/CD histories for startup and oscillations, fixed-phase cycle overlays for repeatability, and the convergence/diagnostic tables for context. A repeatability pass is not a mesh/time/propagation accuracy claim. Failed and incomplete runs retain their labels and diagnostic files.</p>
<h2>What a status means</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Status</th><th>Next action</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Prepared / zero steps</td><td>Geometry or wave definition is ready; it contains no new wave-flow result.</td></tr><tr><td>Paused / saved</td><td>Open the completed .sim or queue a verified continuation.</td></tr><tr><td>Physical stability guard</td><td>Inspect speed, phase and saved location. Preserve the failed attempt and create a controlled diagnostic from an earlier safe state.</td></tr><tr><td>Native phase-mass flag</td><td>Review the mass diagnostic separately. It is not automatically the reason for a physical-speed stop.</td></tr><tr><td>20-period cap</td><td>Save and review why the cycles did not repeat; do not call the result converged.</td></tr><tr><td>Stale lock / interrupted controller</td><td>Check actual processes before recovery. Do not delete locks or restart completed controllers blindly.</td></tr></tbody></table>
<h2>Files and recovery</h2><p>Each case lists the complete calculated .sim path and source identity. Use Copy path or Show folder if your browser blocks a file link. The <a href="chat_rescue.html">Chat rescue page</a> contains an up-to-date copyable handover. It is safe to close the browser; the local controller runs independently.</p><p>Updated """+html.escape(now)+'</p></body></html>'
 rescue=header('Chat rescue handover')+'<p><a href="dashboard.html#manual-control-panel">Local controls</a> · <a href="standalone_control_guide.html">Guide</a></p><h1>Continue with Chat</h1><p>Copy this handover into the next chat. The next agent must read current disk files and process state before any action. No credentials are included.</p><p><button id="copy">Copy handover</button> <span id="copied"></span></p><textarea id="handover" readonly>'+html.escape(text)+'</textarea><p>Local text file: <code>'+html.escape(str(R/'CHAT_CONTINUE_LATEST.txt'))+'</code></p><p>Generated '+html.escape(now)+'</p><script>document.getElementById("copy").onclick=async()=>{const t=document.getElementById("handover");try{await navigator.clipboard.writeText(t.value);document.getElementById("copied").textContent="Copied"}catch(e){t.focus();t.select();document.getElementById("copied").textContent="Selected — press Ctrl+C"}};</script></body></html>'
 for destination in [B,D]:
  destination.mkdir(exist_ok=True)
  for name,doc in [('standalone_control_guide.html',guide),('chat_rescue.html',rescue)]:
   temp=destination/(name+'.tmp');temp.write_text(doc,encoding='utf8');temp.replace(destination/name)
 return dict(message='Current handover and guide updated',file=str(R/'CHAT_CONTINUE_LATEST.txt'))
if __name__=='__main__':print(json.dumps(build()))
